build: 2026-06-26 v10.76.34 (Fix: Safe Mode self-clearing — no lock-in)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notesT: Builds on 10.76.33. CRITICAL fix: your 10.76.33 log showed the app booting
  straight into Safe Mode every launch ("LaunchGuard: SAFE MODE"). The bug: in Safe
  Mode the studio's startup task never runs, so the "healthy" confirm never fired and
  the counter never reset — so once tripped (quitting fast a couple of times while
  grabbing logs did it), EVERY relaunch re-entered Safe Mode until you tapped
  "Continue to Echoel". A perfectly healthy app sat trapped behind the recovery screen.
  Fix: the counter is cleared the instant the recovery screen appears. Safe Mode is now
  a ONE-SHOT speed bump — the next launch goes straight to the studio; if the app ever
  truly crashes again the counter rebuilds and Safe Mode returns after that failure.
  To get out RIGHT NOW on the current build: tap "Continue to Echoel" on the recovery
  screen. After 10.76.34 it self-clears.
  Test: 10.76.34 → relaunch a few times → lands in the normal Studio (no sticky Safe
  Mode); Diagnostics shows "ui branch: STUDIO — startup task running" + the full chain.
